  "result": "I stopped at **VACUOUS** after 3 of the 6 gate runs, because the remaining problem is in the node itself, not in my files. All 9 witnesses pass, and the build, checks and anchoring are clean. The only thing the gate still rejects is one obligation leaf: the pedestrian's speed being above `p.halt_speed_tolerance`.\n\n**Why no scene can exercise it:** the f2 trigger requires `drv.motion.moving_across_carrier` with the same tolerance. By that concept's contract the pedestrian is already moving faster than that tolerance at that moment. So wherever the rule applies, the f4 speed test is already true and can never decide anything. The node's own `branch_1` scene shows what was intended (a pedestrian who halts has yielded). Under this trigger, though, a halted pedestrian is simply outside the rule rather than complying by halting.\n\n**Fix for the plan agent** (also in `task_result.md`), one of:\n- **(a)** Drop `kin.speed` from f4, so \"shall yield\" means no contact and no projected conflict while crossing.\n- **(b)** Rewrite f2 so the rule still applies to a pedestrian who has stopped mid-crossing, for example crossing motion seen over a recent time window. The speed test would then separate halting from walking on.\n\n**Gate runs:**\n1. **UNUSED_CLAIM:** I ran it on the untouched skeleton, so this run was wasted.\n2. **VACUOUS** on two leaves, the speed test and the closest-approach distance. I added `branch_5`, where a car passes behind the pedestrian: their centres approach within 3 s but stay about 4.3 m apart.\n3. **VACUOUS** on the speed leaf only.\n\nThe rule follows the record exactly and I declared no narrowings. On top of the planned scenes I added four:\n- `branch_2`: an unlaned roadway, so the roadway itself is the thing crossed.\n- `branch_3`: a pedestrians-prohibited sign governs the roadway, so the rule does not apply.\n- `branch_4`: the pedestrian touches a stopped car with no approach projected, so contact alone decides.\n- `branch_5`: the distance case above.\n\nFiles are in the working directory:\n- `library/TrafficSpec/Rules/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_30_060_A.lean`\n- `library/TrafficSpecWitness/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_30_060_A.lean`\n- `task_result.md`",
